meta {
  name: Set status
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

put {
  url: {{URL}}/v1/admin/virtual-keys/:id/status
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: 01a0c31c-d26e-7a83-a7c6-ba212d9974a5
}

body:json {
  {
    "is_active": true
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Revoke and revive in one endpoint. `true` brings a key back, `false` takes it down.
  
  The budget moves with the key: `bound` on revive, `released` on revoke. The key
  cache is updated in the same call, so the change is live immediately rather than
  waiting for the next 10s sync.
  
  **Reviving is refused** if the budget was rebound to another active key while
  this one was down — one budget funds one live key. Release the other key first.
  
  `is_active` is required. Omitting it is a 400, not a default to false.
  
  Routing changes do not belong here — use Update routing. This endpoint only
  moves the key between live and revoked.
}
